Subject: Name audit_cluster.sh by full path so a kanban worker can run it

Why: the command names the script relative to the skill folder. A kanban worker starts in its card's workspace, where `scripts/audit_cluster.sh` names nothing and the shell exits 127. The full path under the platform profile home resolves from any working directory.
Local-Issue: #3219
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: upstream names the script by a path that resolves outside the skill folder

diff --git a/SKILL.md b/SKILL.md
--- a/SKILL.md
+++ b/SKILL.md
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ script.
 **Command:**
 
 ```bash
-scripts/audit_cluster.sh <cluster-name> <region> <project-id>
+/opt/data/profiles/platform/skills/gke-workload-security/scripts/audit_cluster.sh <cluster-name> <region> <project-id>
 ```
 
 ### 2. Configure Workload Identity (legacy GSA impersonation)
